      "type": "frame",
      "id": "RjikG",
      "x": 25680,
      "y": 60,
      "name": "x-visual-diff-pages — Pages: visual-diff console",
      "width": 3720,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 40,
      "padding": 56,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "tPOAG",
          "name": "Board Header",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hau8C",
              "name": "Kicker",
              "fill": "$marker",
              "content": "x-visual-diff-pages",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LYiyO",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ink",
              "content": "Pages — visual-diff console",
              "fontFamily": "$font-display",
              "fontSize": 40,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "MpfrV",
              "name": "Sub",
              "fill": "$ink-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1000,
              "content": "apps/visual-diff-ui — not part of @gate/blog's capture matrix. Three routes, desktop 1280 / mobile 390 × light/dark, plus the comparison-modal state. The a11y bucket leads the report: is anything inaccessible? before did anything move?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "zdoNh",
          "name": "Section Console — /",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 14,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KafCd",
              "name": "st",
              "fill": "$ink",
              "content": "Visual-diff console — /",
              "fontFamily": "$font-display",
              "fontSize": 24,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PTGHo",
              "name": "note",
              "fill": "$ink-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1000,
              "content": "CURRENT JOB carries a ghost IconButton that dismisses the run on the card — the panel answers with the LAST run when nothing is running, so this is the only way back to the empty state drawn here. It is present only while a FINISHED run is showing: absent on a fresh instance, and absent while a job is running. A dismissal is browser-only and keyed on the job id — the history row, the log and the report are untouched, and the next run brings the card back. REPORTS rows carry the report page's bucket chip row under the id, every bucket and total, zeros included, a11y first when non-empty. A chip opens the report filtered to that bucket; total opens it unfiltered. The chips only navigate, so they stay on a console that draws no delete. SCREENSHOT SETS marks a set whose sha a newer set has captured again with a neutral same-sha badge under its sha, on every capture but the newest, so a second capture of one commit reads as a repeat rather than as a change; a set captured from a dirty tree carries its warning dirty badge under its label. Each mark sits under the value it qualifies, so neither costs the label its width.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
